The build broke because Step 3 (wiring the notification into the REPL) was left incomplete. I fixed it:

1. `src/repl.rs:1331` — the second `PostPromptContext initializer (in the auto-continue loop) was missing the spawn_tracker field that the struct now requires. Added spawn_tracker: &spawn_tracker`.

2. **src/repl.rs `handle_post_prompt** — the spawn_tracker field was never actually *read* (the source of the dead_code/never read` clippy errors). Added the post-turn peek that surfaces finished background spawns:
   ```rust
   for line in ctx.spawn_tracker.newly_finished_background() {
       eprintln!("{DIM}  {line}{RESET}");
   }
   ```
   This is inside the !is_quiet() block right after contextual_hint, so it runs once per turn as specified.

3. **`src/commands_spawn.rs`** — added the 4 tests from the task's Tests section (which were never written): completed-reports-once, skips-running, reports-failed, and the paired negative for foreground spawns.

The `notified field and newly_finished_background()` method were already implemented correctly (with proper char-boundary-safe truncation) — they just weren't being consumed. All four checks pass: build, test (88 + 4 new = 92), clippy with -D warnings, and fmt.
